# Kept with CRLF in the repository too: GitHub serves the stored bytes, and cmd.exe misreads a
# batch file with LF line endings and UTF-8 text (it ran the comments as commands).
*.cmd -text
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
*.sh text eol=lf
# The voices (Ceci, Luke, João): each reference clip and its transcript are cloned on every machine
# exactly as stored, never converted, so every install speaks with the same voice (hub/engine.test.mjs
# pins their sha256).
*.wav binary
agent/ceci-voice.txt -text
agent/luke-voice.txt -text
agent/joao-voice.txt -text
